DTSTAMP:20261023T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261027T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261027T170000
SUMMARY:LEGO Fun Tuesday at Semmes
LOCATION:Semmes Regional Library\, 9150 Moffett Road
DESCRIPTION:Tuesdays · 4:00 PM to 5:00 PM\n\nSemmes Regional Library runs 
 a LEGO building challenge meant to encourage imagination alongside buildin
 g skill\, for ages 6 through 18. It meets Tuesdays at 4 PM\, including Oct
 ober 6\, 20 and 27. On October 13 it becomes LEGO Haunted Tuesday\, with b
 uilding while watching Lego Scooby-Doo Haunted Hollywood.\n\nPrice: No pub
 lished price\n\nDetails: https://coastaleventures.com/events/ev-lego-fun-t
 uesday-at-semmes-0908.html
URL:https://coastaleventures.com/events/ev-lego-fun-tuesday-at-semmes-0908.
 html
CATEGORIES:STEM and learning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev_nwfaa_astronomy_workshop_crestview_1027-2026-10-27@coastaleventures.
 com
DTSTAMP:20261023T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261027T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261027T180000
SUMMARY:NWFAA Astronomy Workshop at Crestview Library
LOCATION:Crestview Library\, 1445 Commerce Dr\, Crestview\, FL 32539
DESCRIPTION:Tuesday 10/27 · 5:00 PM to 6:00 PM\n\nThe Northwest Florida Am
 ateur Astronomers Association meets at Crestview Library for an hour of sk
 y talk that supports the library's loan-a-telescope program. The group cov
 ers astronomical objects and events visible over the next 30 days\, recent
  astronomy news and general questions. The listing marks it for families a
 nd everyone\, and the workshop is free.\n\nPrice: Free\n\nDetails: https:/
 /coastaleventures.com/events/ev-nwfaa-astronomy-workshop-crestview-1027.ht
 ml
URL:https://coastaleventures.com/events/ev-nwfaa-astronomy-workshop-crestvi
 ew-1027.html
CATEGORIES:STEM and learning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev_makerspace_studio_fall_2026_0923-2026-10-28@coastaleventures.com
DTSTAMP:20261023T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261028T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261028T193000
SUMMARY:Makerspace Studio Fall 2026
LOCATION:Downtown Pensacola\, Museum of Commerce\, 201 E Zaragoza St\, Pens
 acola\, FL 32502
DESCRIPTION:Wednesdays · 5:30 PM to 7:30 PM\n\nThis hands on course at the
  Museum of Commerce in downtown Pensacola covers 3D printers\, laser engra
 vers\, CNC mills\, sewing\, electronics\, and other fabrication tools. No 
 prior experience is required\, and it meets Wednesday evenings from 5:30 P
 M to 7:30 PM\, September 23 through November 4\, with no class October 7. 
 Tuition runs $215 per person.\n\nPrice: from $215\n\nDetails: https://coas
 taleventures.com/events/ev-makerspace-studio-fall-2026-0923.html
URL:https://coastaleventures.com/events/ev-makerspace-studio-fall-2026-0923
 .html
CATEGORIES:STEM and learning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
